{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"852744696979128330","content":"Spin Up\nBefore you make an attack with the chaingun, it must spin up. This takes a bonus action. Once the chaingun is spinning, it remains spinning until the end of your next turn in which you do not attack with it.\n\nVoltaic Volley- uses 10 rounds of ammunition\nGun down a single foe with a flurry of galvanized rounds. Make an attack roll on hit; they take 4d4 lightning damage and must make a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or lose their reaction til the end of your next turn.\n\nLightning Shackles- uses 20 rounds of ammunition \nBolts of lightning spray from the barrels as you pull the trigger on the spun up gun. You choose up to 5 targets that are all within at least 15 feet of one of the other targets. They must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, they take 4d8 Lightning damage and are restrained as the electric current surges through their body’s, or half as much and suffer no other ill effects on a success.(edited)\n\nStatic Burst- uses 10 rounds of ammunition\nAs a reaction to getting hit by an attack and as long as the chaingun is spun up, you can make all creatures within 5ft of you make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw. Taking 2d8 lightning damage and disadvantage on the next attack they make on a failure or half as much and no disadvantage on a success. After using this you need to Spin Up again.","created_at":"2021-07-29T20:59:52.531000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"870410323360882718","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
